    SUB-CLASS NARROWING (board #778) — the screen can now hold a PARTIAL claim (`CfgClass{class, Whole | Keys(&[..])}`), and this is the bracket that keeps a restriction NARROWER OR EQUAL rather than wider. `admits` is `class == class && <sub>`, so `Keys` only ever CONJOINS: a restriction can remove an admitted (class,key) pair and never add one. That is algebra; these four numbers are the measurement, re-derived from this scan's own frontier. BOTTOM 0 ⊆ ENUMERATED 119 == SHIPPED 119 ⊆ TOP 139, of 140 frontier TUs (11 classes in TOP, 252 (class,key) pairs enumerated).
